{"content_hash": "fbf34b6d23c68797", "version_id": 141, "article_id": 15, "level_code": "en_a1", "lang": "en", "level": 1, "level_label": "A1 入门", "title": "US woman Christa Pike survives failed execution", "title_zh": "美国女子克里斯塔·派克注射死刑失败后活了下来", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8kgezxn54qko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/226c/live/7221efd0-c1c9-11f1-b8a9-47f21beea0a3.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 146, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "Christa Pike is a prisoner in the US. She was on death row. Last week, she survived a failed execution. Now she is awake and speaking.", "lead_zh": "克里斯塔·派克是美国的一名囚犯。她原本要被执行死刑。上周，一次死刑执行失败，她活了下来。现在她醒了，还能说话。", "preview": "Pike is 50 years old. She is in a hospital. She is handcuffed to a bed. Her lawyers say she is awake and speaking. She is still very sick. S", "preview_zh": "派克今年50岁。她住在医院里。她被铐在床上。她的律师说，她醒了，还能说话。她仍然病得很重，需要很多医疗照顾。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 131, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/audio/15/en_a1.mp3", "duration": 60.788, "size_bytes": 368496, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 168, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@17fa5ff/content/data/versions/141.json", "paragraphs": ["Pike is 50 years old. She is in a hospital. She is handcuffed to a bed. Her lawyers say she is awake and speaking. She is still very sick. She needs a lot of medical care.", "Last Wednesday, the state of Tennessee tried to kill Pike. They used a drug called pentobarbital. But the drug did not work. Pike did not die. She was unconscious for many days.", "Pike killed a woman named Colleen Slemmer in 1995. She was 18 years old then. A judge said she must die for her crime. Now, the governor of Tennessee stopped all executions for the rest of the year.", "Experts say this is very unusual. Almost everyone who gets this drug dies. Pike is the only person who lived. Her lawyers say she has bad damage to her arms. They do not know how long her recovery will take."], "paragraphs_zh": ["派克今年50岁。她住在医院里。她被铐在床上。她的律师说，她醒了，还能说话。她仍然病得很重，需要很多医疗照顾。", "上周三，田纳西州试图处死派克。他们使用了一种叫戊巴比妥的药物。但是药物没有起作用。派克没有死。她昏迷了很多天。", "派克在1995年杀死了一个名叫科琳·斯莱默的女人。当时她18岁。法官说，她必须为自己的罪行而死。现在，田纳西州州长停止了今年剩下的所有死刑执行。", "专家说这非常不寻常。几乎所有被注射这种药物的人都会死。派克是唯一活下来的人。她的律师说，她的手臂受到了严重损伤。他们不知道她的康复需要多长时间。"], "body": "Pike is 50 years old. She is in a hospital. She is handcuffed to a bed. Her lawyers say she is awake and speaking. She is still very sick. She needs a lot of medical care.\n\nLast Wednesday, the state of Tennessee tried to kill Pike. They used a drug called pentobarbital. But the drug did not work. Pike did not die. She was unconscious for many days.\n\nPike killed a woman named Colleen Slemmer in 1995. She was 18 years old then. A judge said she must die for her crime. Now, the governor of Tennessee stopped all executions for the rest of the year.\n\nExperts say this is very unusual. Almost everyone who gets this drug dies. Pike is the only person who lived. Her lawyers say she has bad damage to her arms. They do not know how long her recovery will take.", "body_zh": "派克今年50岁。她住在医院里。她被铐在床上。她的律师说，她醒了，还能说话。她仍然病得很重，需要很多医疗照顾。\n\n上周三，田纳西州试图处死派克。他们使用了一种叫戊巴比妥的药物。但是药物没有起作用。派克没有死。她昏迷了很多天。\n\n派克在1995年杀死了一个名叫科琳·斯莱默的女人。当时她18岁。法官说，她必须为自己的罪行而死。现在，田纳西州州长停止了今年剩下的所有死刑执行。\n\n专家说这非常不寻常。几乎所有被注射这种药物的人都会死。派克是唯一活下来的人。她的律师说，她的手臂受到了严重损伤。他们不知道她的康复需要多长时间。", "text": "Pike is 50 years old. She is in a hospital. She is handcuffed to a bed. Her lawyers say she is awake and speaking. She is still very sick. She needs a lot of medical care. Last Wednesday, the state of Tennessee tried to kill Pike. They used a drug called pentobarbital. But the drug did not work. Pike did not die. She was unconscious for many days. Pike killed a woman named Colleen Slemmer in 1995. She was 18 years old then. A judge said she must die for her crime. Now, the governor of Tennessee stopped all executions for the rest of the year. Experts say this is very unusual. Almost everyone who gets this drug dies. Pike is the only person who lived. Her lawyers say she has bad damage to her arms. They do not know how long her recovery will take.", "vocab": [{"word": "prisoner", "pos": "noun", "zh": "囚犯", "note": ""}, {"word": "hospital", "pos": "noun", "zh": "医院", "note": ""}, {"word": "lawyer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "律师", "note": ""}, {"word": "drug", "pos": "noun", "zh": "药物", "note": ""}, {"word": "die", "pos": "verb", "zh": "死", "note": ""}, {"word": "kill", "pos": "verb", "zh": "杀死", "note": ""}, {"word": "unusual", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不寻常的", "note": ""}, {"word": "recover", "pos": "verb", "zh": "康复", "note": ""}], "title_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say", "summary_original": "Experts and lawyers called the apparent recovery unprecedented, noting she is believed to be the only known person to survive a lethal injection.", "body_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say\nBy\nSareen Habeshian\nand\nKwasi Gyamfi Asiedu\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nUpdated 57 minutes ago\nUS death row inmate Christa Pike is \"conscious and speaking\" after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, her lawyers say.\nPike, 50, continues to receive critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital, her attorneys said in a statement on Tuesday.\nPike, who was sentenced to death after murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995, survived two failed lethal injections last Wednesday in Tennessee. She was taken to hospital, where she remained unconscious for days as medical staff cleared her body of the injected chemical.\nExperts and her legal team say her apparent recovery is unprecedented. She is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection.\nHer lawyers called her progress \"medically unprecedented\", and while her prognosis remains unclear, \"at a minimum, we expect a long recovery\".\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist and professor at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking.\nThere were seven other cases where prisoners survived slated executions, but in those cases, executioners were not able to inject anything into the inmates' veins, Denno told the BBC.\nPike \"is the only person for whom some kind of toxin has been injected,\" she said.\n\"They did everything they were supposed to do as part of the execution process, and it simply didn't work,\" Denno said. \"This has never happened before.\"\nAuthorities have not yet said whether they will try again to execute Pike. They have also not offered an explanation for what went wrong after injecting her with the chemical pentobarbital.\nTennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year - and the head of prisons in the state said over the weekend that he plans to resign.\nPike was 18 when she and her then-boyfriend, Tadaryl Shipp, beat, tortured and killed 19-year-old Slemmer, whom they had met at a job training camp for troubled teens.\nPike's attorneys are scheduled to appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. They also plan to hold a news conference outside the court.\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said on Tuesday that the likelihood of recovering from lethal injection is low.\n\"Most people who get lethal injection die from it,\" he told the BBC. \"In fact, pretty well everyone, except Christa. So, the fact that she survived it ... was unusual.\"\nBut there remains a lot of uncertainty and many unknowns, he said, including how much of the pentobarbital got into her system, what her blood levels were after the injection and what her recovery will look like.\n\"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he noted.\nZivot had previously said the two doses of pentobarbital she received last week would have been enough that, had it entered her bloodstream in normal circulation, \"she would have surely died\".\nInstead, Zivot said a possible explanation is that instead of entering Pike's bloodstream, the pentobarbital was more likely to have spread across the tissue under her skin.\nZivot said last week he thought her ending up with a brain injury was \"very possible\", due to the delays in resuscitating her. He also believed it would take about a week to truly understand her condition and do a neurological exam. It's now been six days since the failed attempt to execute her.\nPike's lawyers previously warned that her medical history and anatomy - including thrombocytosis (a blood-clotting condition) and small veins - meant there was a risk she would experience \"unnecessary\" pain and suffering during a lethal injection.\nThey said on Tuesday that she has endured \"severe damage\" to her arms.\nRelated topics\nTennessee\nCapital punishment\nUnited States\nMore on this story\nI interviewed Christa Pike 20 years ago - I can't stop thinking about her\nPublished\n3 days ago\nTennessee prison chief to resign after Christa Pike's failed execution\nPublished\n3 days ago\nWhat happened in the failed execution of Christa Pike - and what next?\nPublished\nJust now", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:57:05.204052", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Pike", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.425, "sm": 100, "em": 425, "cs": 0, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "is", "s": 0.438, "e": 0.6, "sm": 437, "em": 600, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "50", "s": 0.613, "e": 0.81, "sm": 612, "em": 810, "cs": 8, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "years", "s": 0.81, "e": 1.304, "sm": 810, "em": 1303, "cs": 11, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "old", "s": 1.304, "e": 1.6, "sm": 1303, "em": 1600, "cs": 17, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": ".", "s": 1.6, "e": 2.462, "sm": 1600, "em": 2462, "cs": 20, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": 